                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "kk83":</h3><p><b>KK83</b> was Neumann&#8217;s designation for a small-diameter omnidirectional (pressure) capsule introduced in 1965. It used a Mylar diaphragm, and as such represented a significant departure from the metal-diaphragm capsules used at the time.</p><p>The KK83 was the 3rd-generation capsule used in the M50. It was also used in the company&#8217;s successful KM83 microphone.</p>
